# Files the Shopify CLI must not upload.
#
# NOT the same job as .gitignore, and the difference is the whole point:
# .gitignore keeps things out of the REPO, this keeps things off the STORE.
# assets/suf.css and assets/suf.css.map are both gitignored, but git has no say
# in what `shopify theme push` sends -- it walks the working directory.
#
# suf.css.map is ~385 KB, more than three times suf.css itself, and it is of no
# use to a visitor. `npm run dev` writes it, `shopify theme dev` uploads it on
# every rebuild (visible in the dev log as "Synced update assets/suf.css.map"),
# and every push carried it to the live theme. `css:build` uses
# --no-source-map, so the deploy build does not REGENERATE it -- but the stale
# file from the last dev session is still on disk and still gets pushed.
#
# suf.css itself is NOT listed here, deliberately. It is gitignored because it
# is generated and churns, but the store needs it -- a clean clone has no
# compiled CSS, which is why every push script builds first.
assets/suf.css.map
